WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.301
A major blow at the border

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.268
for President Biden.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.571
The Supreme Court ruling that title 42,

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:05.972
a controversial Trump

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.308
era border policy will remain in place

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:11.111
as legal challenges play out its policy.

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:12.779
The Biden administration said

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:13.880
it was ready to see.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.415
And just minutes ago,

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.517
President Biden reacted to the ruling

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:23.089
the court is not going to decide

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.493
on how to proceed,

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.029
but I think it's overdue.

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:31.197
But for now, the five to four ruling

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.433
is a major victory for GOP led states

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.801
that asked the Supreme Court

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.403
to step in, like Arizona,

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:37.904
whose attorney general said

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:38.671
he was, quote,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.373
proud to lead the charge

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:42.042
on this important issue.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.943
The policy lets federal officials

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:46.346
quickly expel migrants who cross the U.S.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:47.180
border illegally.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.448
And today's ruling

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.683
means it will continue to take place

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.752
for at least several more months.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.354
It was put in place

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.022
during the beginning of the pandemic

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.424
to stop the spread of COVID.

00:00:57.424 --> 00:00:59.225
But the White House did not want to keep

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.727
the policy, despite warnings

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.762
from Homeland Security officials

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.563
that lifting

00:01:03.563 --> 00:01:06.633
it could lead to disaster at the border.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.234
One source telling CNN

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:11.971
DHS projected between 9000 to 14,000

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:13.173
migrants would try

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:14.441
to cross the southern border

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:15.775
each and every day,

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:16.709
more than double

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.611
the current number of people crossing,

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.480
according to a source familiar

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.781
with those projections.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.049
The White House tonight

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.285
also vowing to comply with the ruling,

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.153
but urging Republicans to now

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.388
work with Democrats

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:30.757
on bipartisan immigration reform.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.125
We've got the story covered

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:33.159
from all angles.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.561
Leila Santiago is near

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:36.096
the border in El Paso, Texas.

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:36.696
And Priscilla

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:38.731
Alvarez is in Washington for us.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.699
We're going to start at the border

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.400
with Leila.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.101
Leila,

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.669
knowing that border officials

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:43.336
have been warning

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.904
of a massive surge of people

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:46.506
coming over the border.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:47.674
If the court allowed

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.642
the removal of Title 42,

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.244
what is the mood there tonight?

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:51.911
What are you hearing

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.381
Well, listen, as I've been speaking

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.683
to the migrants themselves,

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.251
I can't stop thinking about one mother

00:01:58.251 --> 00:01:59.552
who just repeated over

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:02.122
and over in Spanish saying, this is bad.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:03.189
This is bad.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.124
She's from Venezuela,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.792
spent months trying to get up here

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.594
and says she tried to cross illegally

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.662
but couldn't because of Title 44.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.631
Then you had the city officials

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:13.733
who had some contingency plans

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.435
in case this was lifted

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.769
and expecting a large surge.

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.571
They're actually still moving forward

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:19.539
with some of those plans

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.240
because they see

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.608
what's on the other side of the border,

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.643
which is a lot of migrants waiting.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:25.178
And then they're dealing with this.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.513
Take a look behind me.

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.381
These are a lot of the migrants

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.483
that have already cross.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.719
And many of these migrants

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:35.255
will not go to the shelters

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.090
or get on a bus out of fear.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.525
They don't want to be moved

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.692
because they don't know

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.693
where they will go.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:41.528
Even though

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:42.629
El Paso city officials

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.064
say they have the capacity right now

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:46.599
to accommodate them.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:48.168
So many of them are here.

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.836
And I'm seeing young men,

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:51.037
I'm seeing older men,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.640
I'm seeing children talk idlers.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:54.974
One of the shelter

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.010
organizers told me that he didn't.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.111
He said that this decision

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.245
by the Supreme Court

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:02.148
will only extend the bottleneck

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:02.682
that we see

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:03.883
at the border right now

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.519
and could create unsustainable pressure

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.154
for law enforcement.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.189
So a lot of folks

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.524
still sort of trying to make sense

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.126
of what this will mean

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.028
for the migrants themselves.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.829
It has really left them

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.965
with a sense of uncertainty and fear.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:20.133
Sara. All right.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.000
Thank you so much, Leila

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.736
Santiago there at the border in El Paso.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.505
Now let's go to CNN White House

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.006
correspondent Priscilla Alvarez.

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:27.974
Priscilla,

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.542
what else are you hearing from

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.543
the White House tonight?

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.511
There is obviously

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.813
a bit of disappointment That's right.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:34.581
And the White House says

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.182
that they will comply with the order,

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:38.051
but they're also pointing the finger

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:38.585
at Congress.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.352
Let me just read part

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.320
of that statement to you.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.421
They said, quote,

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:43.656
Title 42 is a public health measure,

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.025
not an immigration enforcement measure,

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.961
and it should not be extended

00:03:47.961 --> 00:03:48.795
indefinitely.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:49.729
They later went on to say

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:50.964
that today's order

00:03:50.964 --> 00:03:52.031
gives Republicans

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:52.599
and Congress

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:53.800
plenty of time to move

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.802
past political finger-pointing

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.604
and join their Democratic colleagues

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.806
in solving the challenge at our border

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:00.640
by passing

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.242
the comprehensive reform measures

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:02.976
and delivering

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.210
additional funds

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.211
for border security

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.946
that President Biden has requested.

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:08.014
Now, Sara,

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:08.881
this is an issue

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.017
that has vexed Congress for decades

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:11.484
and is

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.085
It is also

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.219
one that has only grown

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:15.822
more politically contentious over time.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.257
So any reform or attempt

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:17.957
to overhaul

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:18.992
the immigration system

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:21.027
is going to be a challenge

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:21.961
in the meantime, though,

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:22.862
the administration says

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:23.863
they're going to move forward

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:25.231
with their preparations

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.099
in the event

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.434
that, as you heard from President Biden,

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.703
title 42 ends next summer.

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:31.971
The Department of Homeland Security

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.573
also saying in a statement

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.408
that migrants should not be listening

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:35.975
to smugglers

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.844
who may try to exploit the situation.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:38.444
Sara. All right.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.145
We have heard

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.413
that there has been some exporting

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.914
going on for sure.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.316
Thank you so much.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:44.384
OUTFRONT now, Scott

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:45.451
Jennings, former

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:46.219
senior adviser

00:04:46.219 --> 00:04:46.719
to Senate

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:47.920
Minority Leader Mitch McConnell

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.789
and a CNN political commentator,

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.257
and Stephanie Rawlings-Blake

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.892
former defense attorney and former

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.861
Democratic mayor of Baltimore.

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:55.795
Thank you both for being here.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:57.997
Good evening.

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.533
Scott, I'll start with you.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.801
What's the big takeaway

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.337
that you see coming out of this

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:06.873
from the Supreme Court's decision?

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:08.107
Yeah, a few things.

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.442
And thanks for having me on tonight.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:10.443
I think, number

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.311
one, the Supreme Court,

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.278
at least temporarily

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:13.780
saved Joe Biden from himself.

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.481
I mean, his administration was in court

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:17.383
arguing to end this.

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.551
And they even admitted in court

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.421
the solicitor general admitted that

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:24.424
lifting Title 42 will lead to disruption

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:25.658
and a temporary increase

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.026
in unlawful border crossings.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:27.694
And we already know

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:28.261
we already

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.362
have a massive number of people

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:30.430
coming across anyway.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.465
So, you know,

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.567
the Supreme Court here did them a favor.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.101
Number two,

00:05:35.101 --> 00:05:36.002
big political win

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:37.537
for the Republicans who run the states

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:38.938
that challenge this.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:40.273
They see what the problem is

00:05:40.273 --> 00:05:41.607
and they wanted to keep this in place.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.409
So I think that was a good move

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.944
politically for the Republicans here

00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:45.545
who were arguing

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:46.713
for more border security.

00:05:46.713 --> 00:05:47.880
But number three,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.881
the real question is going to come

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:51.150
next year. This is going to end.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:53.186
And at what point are all the

00:05:53.486 --> 00:05:54.620
federal policymakers

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.154
going to help

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.456
these states, these governors

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:57.156
and these mayors

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.391
who are dealing with this

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.525
influx of people?

00:05:59.525 --> 00:06:01.127
It's really a federal issue.

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:02.462
They have to secure the border.

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:02.929
And I don't think

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:04.297
the American people think

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.431
everybody coming across

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:06.933
there is a legitimate refugee,

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:07.333
which is what

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:08.868
the position of the Biden administration

00:06:08.868 --> 00:06:10.136
apparently is.

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:12.638
Marilyn's like you think President Biden,

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.774
as well as his predecessors,

00:06:14.774 --> 00:06:15.541
have really failed

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.343
to solve the issue of immigration.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:20.213
And I suspect that includes Congress.

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.482
Do you think this might help

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.217
push two sides together,

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.651
or is this going to be the same old,

00:06:25.651 --> 00:06:26.018
same old

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:27.487
when it comes to Republicans

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:29.155
and Democrats in Congress?

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.359
I think when you listen to Scott

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:34.293
and he talks about it

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:36.062
being a big political win,

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:38.064
that sort of tells you where we are.

00:06:38.064 --> 00:06:39.365
We're talking about people.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.032
We're talking about

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.701
vulnerable populations.

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.871
And too many leaders are still talking

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:46.973
about whether or not we can

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:49.675
who can score political points this

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.778
this is a time of crisis

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.346
that requires leaders

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:53.780
to do

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.882
what they are elected to do

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:57.617
and which is to lead

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:59.552
in difficult circumstances.

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:01.888
And we need more attention.

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:03.089
This is a crisis.

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.590
We need to see members

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.692
of the Biden administration

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:07.593
at the borders

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.528
with mayors

00:07:08.528 --> 00:07:08.928
who are

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.931
on the ground dealing with this issue day

00:07:11.931 --> 00:07:12.732
in and day out

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:15.301
until some real comprehensive

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.769
solutions can be found.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:18.805
And to be fair, we have heard

00:07:18.805 --> 00:07:20.006
and I totally agree

00:07:20.006 --> 00:07:21.140
with with that last statement

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:21.841
that we need to see

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:23.709
the Biden administration at the border.

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:24.610
Neither the president

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.479
nor the vice president has visited

00:07:26.479 --> 00:07:26.913
the border.

00:07:26.913 --> 00:07:28.681
They have not offered the kind of support

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:29.749
to the Border Patrol.

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:31.918
In fact, they have attacked in the past.

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:32.952
Border Patrol agents

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:34.020
who were doing their job.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.054
So I totally agree.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:36.656
I do think we need to see Biden

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:38.357
and Kamala Harris and other officials

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:39.058
down there

00:07:39.058 --> 00:07:40.593
admitting that they have told

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:41.761
the American people

00:07:41.761 --> 00:07:42.995
a bunch of falsehoods they just

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:44.397
made, said the border is secure.

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:45.364
That's not true.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:45.865
White House

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:46.933
press secretary is said,

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.000
oh, people are just

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.602
it's not like they walk across.

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:50.970
That's not true.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.972
It's been dishonest statements

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:54.240
after dishonest statements.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:55.541
And they've never even visited

00:07:55.541 --> 00:07:56.476
the see this crisis.

00:07:56.476 --> 00:07:58.211
So I agree with it. Okay.

00:07:58.211 --> 00:08:00.646
So you both agree on something.

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:03.115
Scott, I want to get quickly to reading

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:03.983
some of what the White House

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:05.685
response to this ruling is.

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:07.019
And in part,

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:07.954
they say, quote,

00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:08.621
Today's order

00:08:08.621 --> 00:08:09.789
gives Republicans in Congress

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:10.890
plenty of time

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:11.357
to move

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:12.859
past political finger-pointing

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:14.494
and join their Democratic colleagues

00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:17.029
in solving the challenge at our border

00:08:17.029 --> 00:08:18.331
by passing the comprehensive

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:20.032
reform measures and delivering

00:08:20.032 --> 00:08:21.400
the additional funds

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.001
for border

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:24.003
security that President Biden

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.605
has requested.

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:26.672
I know for myself,

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.140
from talking to lawmakers

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.108
on the ground there,

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:31.244
some of the council members in El Paso,

00:08:31.244 --> 00:08:32.078
they've said that they're not

00:08:32.078 --> 00:08:33.279
seeing those federal funds.

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:35.047
They need the federal funds

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:37.183
to deal with the influx of people.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.918
Why can't Republicans

00:08:38.918 --> 00:08:40.987
and Democrats seem to come together?

00:08:40.987 --> 00:08:41.320
Is it

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.622
because we are seeing

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:45.057
the edges of both parties

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:46.592
keeping reform from happening,

00:08:46.592 --> 00:08:48.261
keeping major reform from happening?

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:49.929
Well, I think there's

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:51.998
a fundamental deep disagreement

00:08:51.998 --> 00:08:53.132
between both parties

00:08:53.132 --> 00:08:54.734
on who should be able to come

00:08:54.734 --> 00:08:55.701
across and claim

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.236
legitimate refugee status

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:58.771
It appears that the left

00:08:58.771 --> 00:08:59.939
and the Biden administration

00:08:59.939 --> 00:09:01.107
thinks everybody should come

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:01.541
and we should just

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:02.708
do the paperwork faster.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:03.442
And the Republicans,

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.511
I think, want to slow this down and say,

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:06.112
wait a minute, what?

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:06.646
We really need to

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:07.613
focus on

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:09.282
is more resources

00:09:09.282 --> 00:09:10.683
to actually secure the border.

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:11.450
Case in point,

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.251
the other day,

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:13.886
Arizona Governor Doug Ducey

00:09:13.886 --> 00:09:15.421
literally took shipping containers

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:16.622
and tried to build a wall

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.758
on the Arizona border in the Yuma Gap.

00:09:18.758 --> 00:09:20.526
And the Biden administration sued him

00:09:20.526 --> 00:09:22.061
and made him take it down.

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:24.163
So I think the fundamental disagreements

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:25.097
on priorities

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:27.300
here, Republicans for border security,

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:29.569
the Biden administration says come on in.

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:31.070
That's a big divide.

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:31.537
And I and

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:32.305
I have a hard time

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:33.372
seeing how bipartisan

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:34.440
solutions will happen

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.308
when you've got such

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:37.443
fundamental disagreements on the policy.

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:39.145
But I think it's a bit disingenuous

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:39.445
to say

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:40.646
that the Biden administration is saying,

00:09:40.646 --> 00:09:42.114
come on in.

00:09:42.114 --> 00:09:43.583
There are still border agents there.

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:44.984
They are still trying to do their job.

00:09:44.984 --> 00:09:45.518
And what they're seeing

00:09:45.518 --> 00:09:47.520
is a huge influx of people

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.021
who are trying to come in

00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:50.456
and they'll do it any way that they can.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:51.691
Their Rawlings-Blake.

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:53.059
Just curious about your response

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:54.860
to what you heard from from Scott there

00:09:54.860 --> 00:09:56.629
and what you heard from the

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:58.097
from the Biden administration itself.

00:09:59.732 --> 00:10:00.399
You know,

00:10:00.466 --> 00:10:01.601
every day the

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:02.902
Republican Party sends out

00:10:02.902 --> 00:10:03.869
its talking points

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:05.371
on all the news of the day.

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:07.873
The Democratic Party does the same thing.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.041
I get it.

00:10:09.041 --> 00:10:09.909
I get it.

00:10:09.909 --> 00:10:10.509
You know,

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.211
their positions that, you know,

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:14.113
we're supposed to take to say, you know,

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:15.481
the republic

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:17.083
is a fundamental disagreement.

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:18.584
Of course, there's a disagreement.

00:10:18.584 --> 00:10:19.518
There's a lot of things

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.687
that I'm sure that if we sat down,

00:10:21.754 --> 00:10:23.055
we could agree on.

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:26.792
But until the leaders who are elected

00:10:26.792 --> 00:10:28.361
are willing

00:10:28.494 --> 00:10:30.463
to not worry about who gets the blame,

00:10:30.463 --> 00:10:32.431
not worry about who gets the credit

00:10:32.431 --> 00:10:34.800
and try to help these these

00:10:35.768 --> 00:10:37.803
these people who deserve better,

00:10:38.204 --> 00:10:39.238
we're going to be stuck.

